WEBVTT

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.090
Isn't Brother taking a little too much?

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.130
We should take everything we can.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.510
Oh, Biwa!

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.260
Have you packed up what you're bringing?

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:33.260
Yup.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:37.430
Wow, you packed so light!

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:42.310
Ugh, if only Grandfather hadn't gone
and moved the capital to Fukuhara.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:45.480
If we stay here, there might
be another rebellion.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:49.900
But in Fukuhara, we'll have the sea
in front and mountains at our backs.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.610
It'll be easier to protect everyone!

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:53.700
Ow!

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.870
You sure packed light upstairs.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.710
What he wants to protect
is the Heike's power.

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:04.630
The sudden relocation didn't
leave enough time to build homes.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:09.130
But anyone who stays will be
viewed as opposing the Heike.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:14.720
People are dismantling their current
homes to take the timbers with them.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:18.220
The capital will be like a ruin.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:34.150
THE HEIKE STORY

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.940
Episode 6

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.320
Fukuhara is a nice place, too.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.870
Oh, oh, oh.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:02.620
Ah, this feels so nice!

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:08.040
Kiyotsune, I really envy your
ability to empty your head out.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.540
You don't want to play in the water?

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.000
N-Not really.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.880
Liar. Of course you do.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:16.130
Take that.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.010
Are you Lords Sukemori and Kiyotsune?

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.560
I am Atsumori, the youngest
son of Taira no Tsunemori.

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.480
I don't recognize him.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.190
His father is Grandfather's brother.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:33.150
When I visited the estate,
I was told you were out here.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.990
You didn't need to come
out here to greet us.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:38.860
I very much wished to meet Lord Kiyotsune.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:39.910
<i>Him</i>?

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:40.910
Oh, yes!

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.250
I have heard Lord Kiyotsune
is a master of the flute.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:48.750
That's the famous flute
known as Saeda, right?

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:53.090
The one your grandfather
received from Emperor Toba?

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:53.880
Yes.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:57.420
I would just love to
hear you play, Atsumori.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.930
I feel the same about you.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:05.390
Then why don't we meet here
tonight for some moon viewing?

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:06.980
Oh, how elegant!

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.620
What a lovely moon.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.080
A lovely moon indeed.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.670
Although this comes late, I offer my
condolences about your father.

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:38.010
To think it has already been a year...

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:43.680
I greatly respected Lord Shigemori's
accomplishments as a warrior.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.180
Especially his speech
in the Heiji Rebellion:

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.140
"The era is Heiji, the capital is Heian,
and we bear the Hei name!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.900
All use the 'hei' character!

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.020
So let us pacify the enemy!"

00:04:54.020 --> 00:05:00.400
I listened with rapture to the tales of
him and how he roused his fighters.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:04.660
My father would be pleased to hear that.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:08.040
Did we come here to just
flap our gums like that?

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:10.540
Or to hear the flute?

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:12.540
My apologies!

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:17.170
My brother can be a little negative
sometimes. Just ignore it.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.390
Now then.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.220
Room for one more?

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.560
Lord Shigehira!

00:05:28.930 --> 00:05:31.100
Lord Shigehira, I am--

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.310
I know.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.690
Truly?

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:37.230
I have heard of your accomplishments,
Lord Shigehira!

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:41.780
I heard you performed magnificently
in the battles at Uji and Onjoji Temple.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:48.370
War talk will put a cloud
over our fine moon.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:51.120
Now, let me hear the famed Saeda.

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:52.120
Yes.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:37.580
This place is so small that I hear that
everyone calls it the "Cage Palace."

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:42.090
I will ask my father to let you
move somewhere more spacious.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:45.180
As if that darned Kiyomori
would acquiesce.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:49.260
For now, please patiently
endure it a while longer.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:54.560
Clarity of heart and mind arises at the
sight of a collapsed temple in a field.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.270
Oh, that's part of an <i>imayo</i>.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.560
Yes.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:04.360
If it is only for a while, I suppose
even the Cage Palace could be fun.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.780
I hear that the retired
emperor feels unwell.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:13.200
Oh, yes. Perhaps the fatigue of
the sudden relocation set in.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:25.380
You do not need to trouble
yourself with that.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:26.800
It is no trouble.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.760
I am sorry.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.600
You have no reason to apologize.

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:34.020
Then I will say, "I am grateful."

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:38.650
You do not need to... to be so
overly considerate with me.

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:43.190
I hear you are even making
visits to Father.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:53.200
I have been making you take care of me
ever since you joined me at my young age.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:08:01.290
You were beautiful and intelligent.
I admired you.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.420
I was embarrassed that I, in contrast,
knew nothing of the world

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.130
and could do nothing.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:11.180
I am thankful for you.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:18.230
It makes me happy to know
you felt that way about me.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:27.490
There, there.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:30.530
He starts crying when he hears the waves.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:34.220
And this is how Grandfather
stared down the skull.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:40.930
And there are apparently tons
of other strange occurrences.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:43.140
A pine tree withered in a single night,

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:47.770
and a mouse made a nest in the tail of
finest horse in the eastern provinces.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:50.400
I heard it even bore its young there.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.530
What on earth?

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.660
Brother is a scaredy-cat, so...

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:58.660
I would gladly take spirits over...

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:10.130
I hear your father is a skilled poet.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:13.170
You should come to his
next poetry contest.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:19.600
I bet there are so many stories about
spirits because it's way lonelier here.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:22.930
People want to go back to the capital.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:27.520
Is that woman you fancy
still in the capital?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:31.230
Aren't you good at poetry?
You could send a letter.

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:37.620
You may not understand, but relationships
between men and women aren't so simple.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:41.040
If I can't see her, my only option
is to get a fine bride.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:43.910
I can't believe you.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.040
Excuse me.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.250
Lord Kiyomori calls for you.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.460
For Biwa?

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:51.760
That is correct.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:02.560
What's this? Koremori and Sukemori too?

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.390
You two came out of
concern for Biwa, right?

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.440
I-I came because Sukemori asked me to.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:11.070
"Concern?"

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:16.490
You thought there's no telling
what he might do to Biwa.

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:22.410
Give me a break. I only wanted to calm
the spirits with some biwa music.

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.750
Oh, is that so?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:33.630
I sleep quite soundly,
so I never see any spirits.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.550
I shall go ahead and retire now.

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:39.140
Now, will you play?

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:56.610
This is the music Shigemori listened to.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:01.320
He was a boring man,

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:05.950
but he's the only one who never
shrank from telling me something.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.920
He still had so much left to accomplish.

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:14.090
The aristocrats would spend money
they didn't have and do nothing.

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:18.010
When uprisings occurred in the provinces,
they couldn't even quell them.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:23.220
The world was run by useless
nobles and haughty priests.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.890
Status and authority were everything.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:27.890
We changed that!

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:32.940
We brought air to a stifling world--
through wealth and might!

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:36.280
What is it?

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:40.950
B-But, we Heike are currently...

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:47.750
Whenever great change occurs,
there will be those who oppose it.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:51.210
There will be those who reject change.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:55.630
That is why our clan, the Heike,
must work together as one!

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:05.350
In this new capital, in this open port,
we will build further wealth!

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:08.480
With that wealth, we'll also accrue might!

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:12.150
Thus, our new world will continue.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:16.610
This is your father's skull,
Lord Yoritomo.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.610
My father's?

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:25.990
After the Heiji rebellion, it lay covered
in moss in front of the prison.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.580
I took possession of it.

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:32.210
How frustrated he must have been
with no one to pray for him.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:36.210
Is this truly him?

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:40.920
Prince Mochihito perished in his
aim to bring down the Heike.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.470
Yorimasa and Nakatsuna committed suicide.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:47.930
You are the only one who
can take on their mission!

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:50.810
The Heike claims it created
a new world of warriors,

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:53.190
but they just took the court's place!

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.230
Only their clan members prosper!

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.070
That is... true, but...

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:02.530
Just think how you could
change things, Lord Yoritomo.

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:08.030
Unlike Kiyomori, I could promote
warriors outside my clan,

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:11.830
and create a new world even
while preserving the court.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:15.330
Many would follow you for that!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:20.510
But Lord Kiyomori spared my life.

00:14:20.510 --> 00:14:22.670
To raise troops against him...

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:24.340
Worry not!

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:29.890
I visited Fukuhara and have come with
a decree from Emperor Go-Shirakawa.

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:36.810
The Heike has taken to ignoring
the court and governs selfishly.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.770
Bring the Heike to ruin.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:41.150
Drive off the enemy of the court.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:46.700
Is this genuine?

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:48.450
It is indeed genuine.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:52.330
Yoritomo is raising an army?!

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:56.540
He left Izu with his father-in-law,
Hojo Tokimasa.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.500
I exiled him and spared
him from execution!

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:02.420
How dare he forget his debt to me!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:07.590
However, the report is he engaged
Heike forces at Ishibashiyama and lost,

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:10.220
fleeing with seven or eight riders.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:13.890
We must strike him before
the other Genji rally to him.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:17.730
Got it!

00:15:17.730 --> 00:15:19.730
The commander will be Koremori!

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:20.770
But that's...

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:22.400
Isn't it too soon?

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:27.700
Shigemori had accomplished
great feats at Koremori's age.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.410
Koremori can do it, too.

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:31.910
We will show them the power of the Heike!

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:44.340
Wait for the Genji here?

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:48.640
Would it not be better to cross
the river and Mount Ashigara

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:51.890
to fight in the open eastern fields?

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:56.850
I, Tadakiyo, have been entrusted with
deciding strategy by Lord Kiyomori.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:59.060
The soldiers and horses are tired.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:02.860
As we are also short on provisions,
it's better to wait here.

00:16:04.780 --> 00:16:08.950
We have gathered 70,000 riders.

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.450
I believe it best to move carefully.

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:13.030
Report, sir.

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.370
The Genji have 200,000 riders!

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.330
200,000?!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:20.630
A month has passed since
Yoritomo raised his army.

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:24.090
Genji warriors must have hastened
from all over to join him.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:25.960
Sanemori.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:26.840
Yes, sir?

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.630
I hear you are familiar
with the eastern warriors.

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:33.220
Yes, I often fought alongside the Genji.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:35.470
What are they like?

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.730
They are fierce and spirited.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:40.400
They never fall from their horses.

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:43.230
Whether their parent or child is shot,

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.070
they ride over the corpse
and continue fighting.

00:16:47.780 --> 00:16:53.740
Oh, but none of their warriors can
wield a powerful bow like you, right?

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:59.040
No, the Genji have many archers who
can pierce two or three suits of armor

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:00.170
in one shot.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:05.800
The Genji of Kai and Shinano
provinces know this area well.

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:10.090
I suggest you stay vigilant
to avoid having them flank us.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:16.260
Why did you say those things?

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:20.020
I could see the troops were unmotivated.

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:21.600
I wanted to rouse them.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.650
Because their lives are easier,

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:28.070
the Heike warriors have
lost their past ferocity.

00:17:28.070 --> 00:17:29.440
Hey, what is that?

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:31.700
Look!

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.450
How could this be?

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.330
This many soldiers...

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:43.380
In the river and the sea, too!

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:47.050
The exchange of arrows
will happen in the morning.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:49.590
They won't attack tonight.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:50.590
Get some rest.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:07.520
♪ In the middle of that night, ♪

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:11.610
♪ the waterfowl that were
present in many flocks... ♪

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:18.080
♪ ...must have been
startled by something. ♪

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:26.290
♪ The furious beating of their
wings all at once ♪

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:29.710
♪ sounded like a gale or thunder. ♪

00:18:34.720 --> 00:18:36.970
♪ "Ah! The Genji draw near!" ♪

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:39.850
♪ "If they surround us, we're finished!" ♪

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:49.520
♪ The Heike warriors scrambled ♪

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:54.030
♪ in a mad dash to escape. ♪

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:05.210
Why did they run without fighting?

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:09.840
They were startled by birds
and fled all at once.

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:11.760
Really?

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:15.550
How disgraceful! It would be one
thing if you had fought and lost!

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:18.970
Koremori, with Shigemori gone,
you lost your backing,

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:22.180
so I wanted to give you some achievements!

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:24.140
That's why I made you commander!

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:27.940
Tadakiyo will be executed!

00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:32.530
Exile Koremori to Kikaigashima!

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:37.700
Father! Lord Tadakiyo is a general who
led the vanguard in the Hogen Rebellion!

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:39.950
He has helped us greatly!

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.490
I must speak as well.

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:48.120
Koremori is not yet used to war. He is
sure to accomplish great things later.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.170
Our enemy is Yoritomo!

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:53.920
Let's unite as a clan to defeat Yoritomo!

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:02.060
He avoided exile, but I must admit
I'm embarrassed as his brother.

00:20:02.060 --> 00:20:03.220
Don't be.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:07.940
When our time to go to war comes,
let's fight bravely and heroically!

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.530
Don't be scared.

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:25.200
You're cute.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.620
I'm Biwa.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:43.930
Koremori.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:48.020
I'm glad y--

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:50.350
I was scared.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:55.900
When I thought about that
number of soldiers attacking,

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:57.110
I was scared.

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:02.070
Koremori.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:04.580
Tonight I'd like to watch you dance.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:06.830
On the beach, like at Itsukushima.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:10.000
No more dancing.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:12.130
The capital changed.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:13.880
I must change, too!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.590
I'll fight.

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:19.510
I have to fight!

00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:21.180
As a Heike warrior!
